<title>COLOMBIA: Colombian peso closes higher at 1,020.25.</title>
<headline>Colombian peso closes higher at 1,020.25.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's peso closed 2.35 higher against the dollar at 1,020.25, buoyed by sales of U.S. currency by banks and exporters, interbank dealers said.</p>
<p>They said demand for dollars caused the peso to close down sharply from its intraday high of 1,016.30, however.</p>
<p>Dealers reported 301 trades for a total of $128 million.</p>
<p>((-- Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
